  I disagree strongly, Jean.

 All natural languages have strong grammatical constructions, some of them
quite bizarre, and we learn them (at least as children) by modelling and
feedback.  Now, might lojban be impossible to learn this way?  Maybe, but
there's really no a priori way of telling.  At the very least, it doesn't
suffer from the cognitive load of having to remember irregularities in verb
or noun construction as natlangs do.  It's easy for an adult to pick up the
grammar of lojban in just a few weeks.

         --gejyspa



